package local:backend;

// A one-case enum, in both positions. It is inhabited -- `only` exists and
// `impl.v` builds it -- but it carries no information, and that is the case
// the backend erases: there is no projection for a field of such a type, no
// test in a `match` on it, and the constructor is built as a heap block
// rather than given the nullary immediate.
//
// So `2*ord+1` does not describe the value, and a lift that halved it
// answered `discriminant 10 out of range [0..1)` from the component boundary
// -- half an address. The lift writes the only discriminant the type has
// instead, which is right under either representation (TODO.md#enum-unit).
//
// `pick` returns `only` rather than its argument on purpose: forwarding would
// hand back whatever the adapter lowered and pass without the backend ever
// building the value.
world wrapper-world {
  use certirocq:abi/errors@0.1.0.{error};
  enum one { only }
  export pick: func(o: one) -> result<one, error>;
}
